Configure: keep a cf_time given with -D

Configure sets cf_time from date(1) after it has read the -D options, so `-D cf_time=...` has no effect and every
build records the moment it was configured (in config.h, Config_heavy.pl, perlbug and perlthanks): two builds of the
same sources differ. With this, a cf_time given is kept; without one, Configure asks date(1) as before.

--- a/Configure
+++ b/Configure
@@ -3917,7 +3917,9 @@
 . ./posthint.sh
 
 : who configured the system
-cf_time=`LC_ALL=C; LANGUAGE=C; export LC_ALL; export LANGUAGE; $date 2>&1`
+case "$cf_time" in
+"") cf_time=`LC_ALL=C; LANGUAGE=C; export LC_ALL; export LANGUAGE; $date 2>&1` ;;
+esac
 case "$cf_by" in
 "")
 	cf_by=`(logname) 2>/dev/null`
